<title>UK: TABLE-SHELL Q2 PROFIT BREAKDOWN.</title>
<headline>TABLE-SHELL Q2 PROFIT BREAKDOWN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to June 30</p>
<p>				(million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Oil and gas		 605		    vs 670</p>
<p> Refining and marketing  449		    vs 475</p>
<p> Chemicals		   182		    vs 185</p>
<p> Coal			   40		    vs   2 deficit</p>
<p> Other			 nil		    vs   3 deficit</p>
<p> Corporate items	   177 deficit	  vs 105 deficit</p>
<p> Minority interests	 29 deficit	  vs  37 deficit</p>
<p>Equity crude oil production (thousand barrels per day)</p>
<p>				2,290		  vs 2,235</p>
<p>Natural gas sales (million cubic feet per day)</p>
<p>				7,012		  vs 7,282</p>
<p>NOTE - Royal Dutch/Shell Group is 60 percent owned by Royal Dutch Petroleum Co of the Netherlands and 40 percent by Britain's Shell Transport and Trading Co.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4365</p>
